{"tool_name":"encyclopedia","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"encyclopedia","version":"2.12.30","home":"https://bitbucket.org/searleb/encyclopedia/wiki/Home","license":"Apache License 2.0","summary":"EncyclopeDIA is library search engine comprised of several algorithms for DIA data analysis","identifiers":["biotools:encyclopedia","doi:10.1038/s41467-018-07454-w"],"description":"EncyclopeDIA is library search engine comprised of several algorithms for DIA data analysis\nand can search for peptides using either DDA-based spectrum libraries or\nDIA-based chromatogram libraries.\nCheck out our manuscript describing EncyclopeDIA at Nature Communications (Searle et al, 2018)\nfor more information. EncyclopeDIA contains Walnut, an implementation of \nthe PECAN (Ting et al, 2017) scoring system, to enable chromatogram library generation\nfrom FASTA protein sequence databases when spectrum libraries are unavailable.\n","build":{"noarch":"generic","number":0},"requirements":{"run":["fonts-conda-ecosystem","openjdk >=11","python"]},"source_url":"https://bitbucket.org/searleb/encyclopedia/downloads/encyclopedia-2.12.30-executable.jar","test":{"commands":["EncyclopeDIA -h | grep -q EncyclopeDIA","EncyclopeDIA edu.washington.gs.maccoss.encyclopedia.Main -scribe -h | grep -q Scribe","EncyclopeDIA edu.washington.gs.maccoss.encyclopedia.Main -walnut -h | grep -q Walnut","EncyclopeDIA edu.washington.gs.maccoss.encyclopedia.Main -thesaurus -h | grep -q Thesaurus","EncyclopeDIA edu.washington.gs.maccoss.encyclopedia.Main -xcordia -h | grep -q XCorDIA","EncyclopeDIA edu.washington.gs.maccoss.encyclopedia.Main -walnut -h | grep -q Walnut","EncyclopeDIA edu.washington.gs.maccoss.encyclopedia.Main -libexport -h | grep -q SearchToLIB"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"encyclopedia","identifiers":["biotools:encyclopedia","doi:10.1038/s41467-018-07454-w"],"license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"EncyclopeDIA is library search engine comprised of several algorithms for DIA data analysis","home_url":"https://bitbucket.org/searleb/encyclopedia/wiki/Home","keywords":["Chromatography, Liquid","Databases, Protein","HeLa Cells","Humans","Peptides","Proteome","Proteomics","Reproducibility of Results","Saccharomyces cerevisiae","Saccharomyces cerevisiae Proteins","Mass Spectrometry","Proteomics experiment","Mass spectrometry"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"EncyclopeDIA","home":"https://bitbucket.org/searleb/encyclopedia/","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"EncyclopeDIA is library search engine comprised of several algorithms for DIA data analysis and can search for peptides using either DDA-based spectrum libraries or DIA-based chromatogram libraries.","addition_date":"2019-06-18T12:42:38Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:23Z","tool_type":["Desktop application"],"version":["0.8.1"],"collections":["Proteomics","ms-utils"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:EncyclopeDIA","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"bsearle@systemsbiology.org","name":"Brian Searle","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bitbucket.org/searleb/encyclopedia/downloads/EncyclopeDIA%20manual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Mass spectrometry spectra","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0943"},"format":[{"term":"SQLite format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3621"}]},{"data":{"term":"Sequence set","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0850"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Peak detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3215"},{"term":"Peptide database search","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3646"},{"term":"Peptide identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3631"},{"term":"Spectrum calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3860"},{"term":"Target-Decoy","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3649"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Peptide identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0945"},"format":[{"term":"Mass spectrometry data format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3245"}]}]},{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Mass spectrometry spectra","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0943"},"format":[{"term":"TraML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3246"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Formatting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0335"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Mass spectrometry spectra","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0943"},"format":[{"term":"SQLite format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3621"}]}]}],"name":"EncyclopeDIA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"vtsiamis","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2018, The Author(s).Data independent acquisition (DIA) mass spectrometry is a powerful technique that is improving the reproducibility and throughput of proteomics studies. Here, we introduce an experimental workflow that uses this technique to construct chromatogram libraries that capture fragment ion chromatographic peak shape and retention time for every detectable peptide in a proteomics experiment. These coordinates calibrate protein databases or spectrum libraries to a specific mass spectrometer and chromatography setup, facilitating DIA-only pipelines and the reuse of global resource libraries. We also present EncyclopeDIA, a software tool for generating and searching chromatogram libraries, and demonstrate the performance of our workflow by quantifying proteins in human and yeast cells. We find that by exploiting calibrated retention time and fragmentation specificity in chromatogram libraries, EncyclopeDIA can detect 20\u201325% more peptides from DIA experiments than with data dependent acquisition-based spectrum libraries alone.","authors":[{"name":"Egertson J.D."},{"name":"Lawrence R.T."},{"name":"MacCoss M.J."},{"name":"MacLean B.X."},{"name":"Pino L.K."},{"name":"Searle B.